EasyMC third-party attributions (MIT / freely reusable agent patterns)
==============================================================================

This file attributes design ideas and patterns adapted under MIT (or equivalent
permissive) terms. EasyMC does **not** vendor the full source trees below; it
reimplements a small subset in Rust for the local Minecraft launcher Agent.

1) earendil-works/pi — Agent loop (MIT)
   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
   Adapted concept: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts
   - Multi-turn LLM ↔ tool execution loop
   - Execute ALL tool_calls in a model turn, append role=tool results, call again
   - Stop when the model returns no tools / final text, or max_turns is reached
   See: crates/easymc-agent/src/agent_loop.rs

2) OpenAI Agents SDK — max_turns / run loop concepts (MIT)
   https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python
   Adapted concept: Runner max_turns style budget for an agent run
   - DEFAULT_MAX_TURNS (6–8) caps model turns per user ask
   - Explicit stop_reason: final_text | no_tools | max_turns | error
   See: crates/easymc-agent/src/agent_loop.rs (AgentLoopConfig / AgentLoopResult)

3) dsh-style skill selection + dangerous-tool guards (docs / pattern reuse)
   Pattern: inject only 1–3 keyword-matched skills into the system prompt
   (do not dump the whole skill library); gate destructive tools behind
   propose/confirm rather than auto-executing in the cloud loop.
   See: crates/easymc-agent/src/skills.rs, is_dangerous_tool in agent_loop.rs,
        skills/*.md, docs/AGENT-LOOP.md

EasyMC itself is MIT — see LICENSE.

4) DaoCloud public-image-mirror — registry prefix map (public service)
   https://github.com/DaoCloud/public-image-mirror
   EasyMC does **not** vendor this repository. It documents the same public
   mirror host prefixes (e.g. docker.m.daocloud.io) in a generated
   containers-registries.conf(5) drop-in for China-friendly Podman pulls.
   See: crates/easymc-container/src/registries.rs, docs/CONTAINER-MODE.md

5) containers/image — registries.conf schema (Apache-2.0)
   https://github.com/containers/image
   EasyMC emits its own TOML drop-in matching the documented schema shape;
   it does not copy Apache-licensed source files from that project.

6) bs-community/skinview3d — 3D skin + cape viewer (MIT)
   https://github.com/bs-community/skinview3d
   Vendored as the npm dependency `skinview3d` (Three.js powered).
   EasyMC wraps it in `src/components/skin-viewer.ts` for wardrobe preview.
   License: MIT — see node_modules/skinview3d/LICENSE

7) LittleSkin CSL public API — China-friendly skin library (service)
   https://littleskin.cn/
   EasyMC does not vendor LittleSkin; it calls the public CustomSkinLoader
   JSON endpoint (`/csl/{name}.json`) and texture hashes for import/preview.
   See: crates/easymc-core/src/skin.rs

